---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Newsletter from '../components/Newsletter.astro';

// Homepage follows the StoryBrand order: hero (want + CTA), stakes, value,
// guide (empathy + authority), plan, explanation, then secondary offers.
const diagnostic = '/chat?topic=flow-diagnostic';

const clients = [
  { name: 'Government of South Australia', logo: '/images/QSA0YC-sa-gov-logo-300x300.jpg' },
  { name: 'SA Power Networks', logo: '/images/8EB93O-sa-powernetworks-logo-300x300.jpg' },
  { name: 'The University of Adelaide', logo: '/images/C9O8I2-uofabw.png' },
  { name: 'Cuscal', logo: '/images/6c914c-screenshot-2023-01-05-at-9.49.22-am.png' },
];

const stakes = [
  {
    title: 'Dates you can’t defend',
    body: 'The board asks when it will land. You give the best date you have, knowing it rests on status reports and hope.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Headcount that doesn’t move the needle',
    body: 'More people go in, yet delivery barely speeds up, because the work is waiting in queues, not short of hands.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Another transformation with nothing to show',
    body: 'New frameworks, new ceremonies, new tools. A year later nobody can show what actually changed.',
  },
];

const outcomes = [
  {
    title: 'See where capacity disappears',
    body: 'Where work waits, how long, and against which shared teams and dependencies. Drawn from the tools you already use.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Forecasts with honest confidence',
    body: 'Delivery forecasts built from your own history, with the range stated plainly instead of hidden behind a single date.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Know which change pays most',
    body: 'Interventions ranked by the capacity they free up, so you decide where to invest before budget is committed.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Only what changes a decision',
    body: 'We measure just enough to make the next call with confidence. No dashboards full of vanity metrics.',
  },
];

const steps = [
  {
    title: 'Connect your delivery data',
    body: 'Read-only access to the tools your teams already use. No new platform to adopt and nothing new for teams to fill in.',
  },
  {
    title: 'See where work waits and what it costs',
    body: 'Within weeks you get a clear picture of your delivery system: queues, dependencies, and the capacity they consume.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Fund the change that frees the most',
    body: 'Act on the highest-leverage change first, track whether it worked, and take the evidence to your board.',
  },
];

const promises = [
  'No new platform to buy or roll out',
  'No scorecards on your people: we model the system, not individuals',
  'Your data stays yours',
];
---
<Base description="Recursive Loop helps technology leaders see where delivery capacity disappears, forecast dates they can defend, and fund the change that frees up the most capacity.">
  <section class="hero">
    <img src="/images/08bb11-recurvise-loop-homepage-web-res-v2.jpg" alt="" fetchpriority="high" />
    <div class="wrap hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">For CIOs and technology leaders</p>
      <h1>See where your delivery capacity goes, and get it back.</h1>
      <p class="lede">We turn the delivery data you already have into a clear picture of where work waits and what that waiting costs, so you can forecast with confidence and invest where it counts.</p>
      <p class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href={diagnostic}>Book a flow diagnostic</a>
        <a class="textlink" href="#how-it-works">See how it works</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="prose">You can see what goes in and what comes out. The trouble is everything in between.</h2>
      <ul class="tiles">
        {stakes.map((s) => (
          <li><strong>{s.title}</strong>{s.body}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section light">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Flow insights</p>
      <h2 class="prose">Run delivery as a system you can see and steer.</h2>
      <ul class="tiles">
        {outcomes.map((o) => (
          <li><strong>{o.title}</strong>{o.body}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap row">
      <div>
        <h2>We know what it’s like to be asked for a date the system can’t support.</h2>
        <p>We’ve spent decades inside delivery organisations, from tightly regulated, safety-critical environments to start-ups, and we’ve seen good leaders forced to steer on gut feel because nobody could show them how work really moves.</p>
        <p>Michael Fagan has been building software for 25 years and holds a degree in Mathematics and an M.Sc. in Machine Learning from Trinity College Dublin. Martin Kearns was one of the first three Scrum Coaches certified by the Scrum Alliance.</p>
        <a class="textlink" href="/our-people">Meet the team</a>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Trusted by</p>
        <div class="logos small">
          {clients.map((c) => (
            <figure>
              <img src={c.logo} alt={`${c.name} logo`} loading="lazy" />
              <figcaption>{c.name}</figcaption>
            </figure>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h2>Three steps to a delivery system you can see.</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        {steps.map((s) => (
          <li><strong>{s.title}</strong>{s.body}</li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <ul class="promises">
        {promises.map((p) => <li>{p}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href={diagnostic}>Book a flow diagnostic</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose-block">
      <h2>Stop steering on instinct.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Most technology leaders are asked to commit dates and budgets for a system they can’t see. So capacity leaks into queues and handoffs, headcount goes up while delivery stays flat, and each new initiative is funded on hope rather than evidence.</p>
      <p>It doesn’t have to be that way. Your teams already produce the data needed to see how work really moves. We read it as a set of signals, not targets, and turn it into forecasts you can stand behind and a ranked list of the changes that would free up the most capacity. You go into the next board conversation with evidence, not optimism.</p>
      <p class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href={diagnostic}>Book a flow diagnostic</a>
        <a class="textlink" href="/insights">Read our thinking on measurement</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section light">
    <div class="wrap row">
      <img src="/images/25be6f-recursive-loop-gen-image-home.jpg" alt="Workshop participants collaborating around a table" loading="lazy" />
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">For your teams</p>
        <h2>Help your teams make the change stick</h2>
        <p>Once you know which change matters most, we help your teams make it: hands-on coaching in DevOps, scaling and team practice, plus accredited Re:Agile training classes.</p>
        <p class="actions">
          <a class="btn" href="/coaching">Coaching</a>
          <a class="textlink" href="/classes">Training classes</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark">
    <div class="wrap row">
      <div>
        <h2>Ideas worth bringing to your next leadership meeting</h2>
        <p class="lede">Short, practical writing on measurement, forecasting and better delivery decisions. Sign up for Re:Agile News.</p>
        <Newsletter />
      </div>
      <img src="/images/11fe58-recurvise-loop-signup-web-res.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { position: relative; background: var(--dark); color: var(--white); min-height: 560px; display: flex; align-items: center; }
  .hero > img { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; opacity: .45; }
  .hero-inner { position: relative; padding-top: clamp(64px, 10vw, 140px); padding-bottom: clamp(64px, 10vw, 140px); }
  .hero h1 { max-width: 15em; }
  .hero .lede { max-width: 34em; }
  .hero .textlink { border-color: var(--white); }
  .eyebrow { font-size: .8rem; letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: .6em; }
  .hero .eyebrow, .dark .eyebrow { color: #e0a3a7; }
  .tiles { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 1.6em 0 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 24px 36px; }
  .tiles li { margin: 0; padding-top: 14px; border-top: 2px solid var(--line); font-size: .98rem; }
  .tiles strong { display: block; margin-bottom: .3em; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .steps { list-style: none; counter-reset: step; padding: 0; margin: 2em 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 28px 40px; }
  .steps li { counter-increment: step; margin: 0; padding-top: 14px; border-top: 2px solid #3a3936; }
  .steps li::before { content: counter(step); display: block; font-size: 2.2rem; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1; color: #e0a3a7; margin-bottom: .3em; }
  .steps strong { display: block; margin-bottom: .3em; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .promises { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 2em; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 28px; color: #b9b6ae; font-size: .95rem; }
  .promises li { margin: 0; }
  .promises li::before { content: '✓'; color: #e0a3a7; margin-right: .5em; }
  .prose-block { max-width: calc(var(--prose) + 2 * var(--gutter)); }
  .logos.small { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 24px; }
  .logos.small img { max-height: 90px; }
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 16px 28px; margin-top: 1.6em; }
  .textlink { font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid currentColor; }
  .textlink:hover { color: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); }
  .dark .textlink:hover, .hero .textlink:hover { color: #e0a3a7; border-color: #e0a3a7; }
  .dark :global(.field input) { border-color: #3a3936; background: #1a1917; color: var(--dark-ink); }
</style>
